through Lauderdale County&#8217;s online tax lien sales, offering up to a 12% interest rate, accessible via <a href=\"https://govease.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">GovEase</mark></a> for a seamless bidding experience from anywhere.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Dive-into-the-Future-of-Investing-in-Lauderdale-County\">Dive into the Future of Investing in Lauderdale County</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>In Lauderdale County, Alabama, Tax Lien Sales offers up to 12% interest, all online, allowing you to bid on tax liens from the comfort of your home. This isn&#8217;t about buying property; it&#8217;s about securing a lien that earns you interest or even leads to property ownership if taxes remain unpaid.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"How-to-Get-Started\">How to Get Started</h3>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"1\" class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Register on GovEase:</strong><br><br><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Create an account on <a href=\"https://govease.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">GovEase</mark></a> and get approved by filling out forms, including a W-9, and arranging your payment method.</span></li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Pre-Bidding:</strong><br><br>Before the auction starts, set your minimum interest rate during the pre-bidding phase. If the property owner redeems the property, you get your investment back plus the interest you bid.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Auction Day:</strong><br><br>The excitement begins as interest rates start at 12% and can go as low as you dare to bid. In case of a tie, a random number generator decides the winner.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Checking Available Properties:</strong><br><br>For a full list of properties, visit <a href=\"https://alproptax.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">alproptax.com</mark></a> in early April.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Key-Details-and-Links\">Key Details and Links</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"></figure>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lauderdale-County-Courthouse-Florence-Alabama.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lauderdale-County-Courthouse-Florence-Alabama-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lauderdale-County-Courthouse-Florence-Alabama-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lauderdale-County-Courthouse-Florence-Alabama-768x512.webp 768w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lauderdale-County-Courthouse-Florence-Alabama-20x13.webp 20w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lauderdale-County-Courthouse-Florence-Alabama-32x21.webp 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lauderdale-County-Courthouse-Florence-Alabama.png\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lauderdale-County-Courthouse-Florence-Alabama.png 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lauderdale-County-Courthouse-Florence-Alabama-541x360.png 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lauderdale-County-Courthouse-Florence-Alabama-296x197.png 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lauderdale-County-Courthouse-Florence-Alabama-768x512.png 768w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lauderdale-County-Courthouse-Florence-Alabama-20x13.png 20w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Lauderdale-County-Courthouse-Florence-Alabama-32x21.png 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-17911 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"Lauderdale County Courthouse Florence Alabama\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Book a Call with Dustin Hahn</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Important-Information\">Important Information</h3>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Tax Lien Auction Date:</strong> May, at 10:00 AM</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Origination and Auction Fees:</strong> A tax lien sold at auction includes a $20 origination cost and a $20 auction fee. The purchaser pays an assignee fee of $5.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Registration:</strong> Bidders must register on the GovEase Auction Portal and submit the necessary documents. The County Revenue Commissioner&#8217;s Office arranges payment.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Interesting-Facts-about-Real-Estate-in-the-County\">Interesting Facts about Real Estate in the County</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Lauderdale County offers a robust real estate market with plenty of investment opportunities. The county provides various properties at tax lien auctions that are ripe for investment. Be sure to explore available properties early for the best opportunities.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Sources\">Useful Links</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://go